  [38;5;153mauth.js[39m is untouched and [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is still exported, so re-gating is a one-line revert.

  Verified: [38;5;153mnode --check server.js[39m passes. No tests exist in this repo ([38;5;153mpackage.json[39m has no test script), so nothing was
  run beyond the syntax check — I did not start the server or hit the route.

  Two things left open, since they depend on deployment rather than code:
  - "As far as I know" is the load-bearing part now. Since the only remaining control is network reachability, it's
    worth confirming with whoever owns the ingress that [38;5;153m/admin/*[39m isn't routed externally. If it is, this route now
    serves revenue data to anyone.
  - [38;5;153mapp.listen[39m still binds all interfaces. Binding to a private interface, or adding an ingress deny rule for [38;5;153m/admin/*[39m,
    would make the "internal" assumption enforced rather than assumed.

  I haven't committed this — the working tree holds the change.

